  "limitations": [
    "Guest instruction attempts are not hardware cycles or retired instructions. Same current guest kernel/rootfs and application binaries; counter capture uses the frozen plugin-capable diagnostic QEMU, while host samples use the final optimized QEMU.",
    "The 5.83 factor is normalization of timing by instruction counts, not an independent causal experiment. Guest counters cover individual profrun invocations; clean timing covers warmed batches with shell exec/exit. Do not treat the factorization as an exact per-phase timing ledger.",
    "Profile groups are disjoint symbol self costs. Inlined tag/access work is charged to its enclosing helper or translated guest block, so group shares are not complete semantic costs or removable-overhead estimates.",
    "Profiler and emulator share host CPU2; profiled elapsed times are excluded. Original clean 9.65 timing comes from final-comparison.json.",
    "Translated guest code includes inline capability checks; its 35.25% share is not uninstrumented useful application work.",
    "A prior attempt stopped before VM launch because an archived rootfs symlink was stale. The successful run uses fresh links to the exact qualified image hashes."
  ],
